{"label":"2A","direction":"supports","claim":"Taiwan's NHRI cut the budget for its outsourced Illumina sequencing lot for 2027 to NT$8.80M, about 15% below the NT$10.34M it awarded for 2026, and its total outsourced sequencing budget fell about 60%.","detail":"NHRI's 2026 open contract (114B0E0213, awarded 26 Aug 2025) had a NT$24,867,926 budget. It awarded NT$10,341,095 for Lot A (Illumina, to Genomics BioSci) and NT$3,989,000 for Lot B (PacBio). The 2027 tender (115B0D0286, published 1 Oct 2026, bids open 14 Oct) has a total budget of NT$9,997,500, split into Lot A Illumina at NT$8,804,000 and Lot B PacBio at NT$1,193,500. The Illumina ceiling is therefore 14.9% below last year's Illumina award (8.804/10.341−1), and the total budget is 59.8% below last year's (9.9975/24.868−1). Awards usually land below budget, so actual 2027 Illumina outsourced spend is likely to fall more than 15%.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=92019239&job_number=115B0D0286","date":"2026-10-01","source_name":"Taiwan Government e-Procurement (PCC) via pcc-api.openfun.app","source_type":"procurement","quote":"Lot 1 (A組) Illumina … 8,804,000元","strength":"strong","why_new":"Known items cover NHRI lots only through 2026; this is the first look at the 2027 tender (Oct 2026)."},
