{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"In Sep 2026, Tri-Service General Hospital (Taiwan's military teaching hospital) bought 16 iSeq 100 reagent sets and 10 NextSeq 500/550 kits, a year after the iSeq 100 reached end of sale. Legacy Illumina reagent tails keep running.","detail":"HJ15568P448 (decided 2 Sep 2026): item 1, iSeq 100 reagent kit, 16 sets at NT$175,500 each (NT$2.808M); item 2, NextSeq 500/550 reagents, 10 sets at NT$82,000 (NT$0.82M). Both are US-origin and were supplied by 瑞林生物科技. Illumina's retirement page puts the iSeq 100 end of sale at 30 Sep 2025, so a hospital was still committing to retired-platform consumables 12 months later. This fits a slow-decaying tail on legacy boxes.","url":"https://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.5.24&job_number=HJ15568P448","date":"2026-09-22","source_name":"Taiwan PCC via pcc-api.openfun.app","source_type":"procurement","quote":"次世代定序系統(iSeq 100)專用試劑套組(或同等品) 16 套","strength":"medium","why_new":"New buyer (Tri-Service/NDMC). Known legacy-tail items cover NTUH's MiSeq and NextSeq contracts, not iSeq buying after end of sale."},
